/* PGY_BUILTIN_NAME_RESERVATION_ROWS
 *
 * A function declared at the top level of a program owns its spelling over a
 * builtin or stdlib operation of the same name, as a local value and a user
 * class already do (docs/205 R7). These spellings are the exception: a
 * top-level function may not take them, on the native and the self-host
 * route alike. The ambient-capability family is not listed here; its rows
 * are builtin_capability_registry.def itself.
 *
 * PGY_BUILTIN_NAME_RESERVED(family, source_name)
 *
 *   RUNTIME_ABI      the runtime declares a C/LLVM symbol with this exact
 *                    spelling, so a program function would collide with it.
 *   RESOURCE         slot, device-slot, view, move and channel operations,
 *                    whose lifetime the resource passes track by this spelling.
 *   STATEMENT_FORM   the typed AST gives a call statement with this callee
 *                    its own statement kind before any name is resolved.
 *   CONSTRUCTOR      the Option and Result constructors are language forms.
 *   TYPED_PROTOCOL   the self-host semantic types the call through the
 *                    builtin's protocol before resolution. This family is
 *                    migration debt: a row leaves it once those owners read
 *                    the declared-callable fact.
 *
 * src/self_hosted/semantic/builtin_shadow_owner.pgy projects the same rows;
 * tests/self_hosted/parity/builtin_name_shadow_owner.sh checks the two and
 * the runtime declarations. Rows are byte-sorted within each family.
 */

PGY_BUILTIN_NAME_RESERVED(RUNTIME_ABI, "Acos")
